# B21: Declarative CRUD Service with Audit & Cache (`spin_crud_service`)

This Stage 3 (`Jenny-Spin v0.4`) benchmark evaluates `@apply(crud::service(table: "accounts", cache_ttl: 300, max_retries: 3))`:
1. **`@apply(crud::service(...))`**: Automatically synthesizes `AccountService.new()`, `create_account(mut self, initial_balance)`, `deposit(mut self, amount)`, `query_summary(mut self)`, and `delete_account(mut self, balance_to_remove)` into `.spun/spin_crud_service.spun.jn`.
2. **`execute_account_batch(init_a: i64, init_b: i64, topup: i64)`**: Creates `var svc = AccountService.new()`, calls `svc.create_account(init_a)?`, `svc.create_account(init_b)?`, `svc.deposit(topup)?`, `svc.delete_account(init_a)?`, and returns `svc.query_summary()`.

```jenny
module spin_crud_service

pub enum ServiceError {
    NotFound,
    DuplicateKey,
    InvalidBalance,
    QuotaExceeded,
}

@apply(crud::service(table: "accounts", cache_ttl: 300, max_retries: 3))
pub struct AccountService {
    pub active_count: i64 = 0,
    pub total_balance: i64 = 0,
    pub cache_hits: i64 = 0,
    pub audit_seq: i64 = 0,
    invariant self.active_count >= 0 && self.active_count <= 1000
    invariant self.total_balance >= 0 && self.audit_seq >= 0
}

pub fn execute_account_batch(init_a: i64, init_b: i64, topup: i64) -> i64 ! ServiceError
    requires init_a >= 0 && init_b >= 0 && topup > 0 else ServiceError.InvalidBalance
    ensures result > 0

@example("EX-B21-01: synthesize CRUD service operations, audit log, and cache counter") {
    val summary = execute_account_batch(100, 200, 50)?
    assert(summary == 25011)

    var svc = AccountService.new()
    svc.create_account(500)?
    assert(svc.query_summary() == 50011)
    assert(svc.audit_seq == 1 && svc.cache_hits == 1)
}

@example("EX-B21-02: enforce CRUD service error guards on missing account and invalid balance") {
    var svc = AccountService.new()
    val empty_dep = svc.deposit(100)
    assert(empty_dep is ServiceError.NotFound)

    val neg_create = svc.create_account(-10)
    assert(neg_create is ServiceError.InvalidBalance)
}
```
